# {{.AppName}}

A Lift-powered serverless API using Pay Theory-style deployment.

## Prerequisites

- Go 1.25 or later
- Node.js 20 or later (for CDK)
- AWS CLI configured with appropriate credentials
- AWS CDK CLI (`npm install -g aws-cdk`)

## Project Structure

```
{{.AppName}}/
├── cmd/api/           # Lambda entrypoint
├── cdk/               # CDK infrastructure
├── dist/              # Build outputs (generated)
├── shell/             # Deployment scripts
│   ├── build.sh       # Build Lambda functions
│   ├── deploy.sh      # Deploy with CDK
│   └── init_env_vars.sh
├── buildspec.yml      # CodeBuild specification
└── lift.yaml          # Lift project configuration
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Initialize environment (edit PARTNER first)
source ./shell/init_env_vars.sh

# Build Lambda functions
./shell/build.sh

# Deploy to dev
./shell/deploy.sh --partner <partner> --stage dev
```

## Deployment

### Using Shell Scripts

```bash
# Deploy to dev
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev

# Deploy to staging
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage staging

# Deploy to production
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage live

# Show what would change (diff)
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command diff

# Destroy deployment
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command destroy

# Bootstrap CDK (first-time setup)
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command bootstrap
```

### Using Lift CLI

```bash
# Build all functions
lift build

# Deploy with partner context
lift up --stage dev --partner mypartner

# Deploy with custom target mode
lift up --stage dev --partner mypartner --target-mode custom

# Destroy
lift down --stage dev --partner mypartner
```

## Stages

| Stage | Domain | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| `dev` | `api.dev.{{.BaseDomain}}` | Development environment |
| `staging` | `api.staging.{{.BaseDomain}}` | Staging/QA environment |
| `live` | `api.{{.BaseDomain}}` | Production environment |

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `PARTNER` | Yes | Partner identifier for multi-tenant isolation |
| `STAGE` | Yes | Deployment stage: `dev`, `staging`, or `live` |
| `TARGET_MODE` | No | Deployment mode (default: `standard`) |
| `AWS_REGION` | No | AWS region (auto-detected if not set) |

## CodeBuild Integration

This project includes a `buildspec.yml` for AWS CodeBuild.

### Required Environment Variables

Set these in your CodeBuild project or CodePipeline:

- `PARTNER` - Partner identifier
- `STAGE` - Target stage (`dev`, `staging`, `live`)
- `AWS_REGION` - AWS region for deployment

### Optional Environment Variables

- `TARGET_MODE` - Deployment mode (defaults to `standard`)

### Required IAM Permissions

Your CodeBuild role needs permissions for:
- CloudFormation stack management
- Lambda deployment
- API Gateway management
- DynamoDB (if used)
- IAM role creation (for Lambda execution roles)
- S3 (for CDK assets)

## Stack Naming

Stacks are named with the pattern: `{{.AppName}}-service-<partner>-<stage>`

Example: `{{.AppName}}-service-mypartner-dev`

## Local Development

```bash
# Run the API locally (requires SAM CLI)
sam local start-api

# Or test individual functions
go run ./cmd/api
```

## Troubleshooting

### CDK Bootstrap Required

If you see "CDK bootstrap required" error:

```bash
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command bootstrap
```

### Build Failures

Check Go module dependencies:

```bash
go mod tidy
go mod verify
```

### Permission Errors

Ensure your AWS credentials have the required permissions. For CodeBuild, verify the service role has the necessary policies.

